https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1457632?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/foolishimp","html_url":"https://github.com/foolishimp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/foolishimp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/foolishimp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/foolishimp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/foolishimp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/foolishimp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/foolishimp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/foolishimp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/foolishimp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/foolishimp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/octet-stream","state":"uploaded","size":61594,"digest":"sha256:7bafef68217b97d5ab4d33ba88b3565f845ec389226f06e55556f4fd7bd1de95","download_count":0,"created_at":"2026-11-14T16:38:55Z","updated_at":"2026-11-14T16:38:55Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/foolishimp/specification_methodology/releases/download/specification_methodology/v3.1.0-rc.1/stdo_toolchain-3.1.0rc1-py3-none-any.whl"}],"tarball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/foolishimp/specification_methodology/tarball/specification_methodology/v3.1.0-rc.1","zipball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/foolishimp/specification_methodology/zipball/specification_methodology/v3.1.0-rc.1","body":"STDO 3.1 connects context construction to the current ticket, supplies default QA → causal triage → appropriate owner re-entry, and introduces Purpose Context as a separate Product. Representation Tools (`a_c`) and STDO Representation now serve visual documentation.\n\nPublic version: **3.1.0**. Exact immutable cut: **3.1.0-rc.1**, published as a normal release under the existing RC identity convention.\n\n- Two purpose indexes target the actual 3.1 native cut: pure/local Python refactoring and SDLC workflow.\n- Codex and Claude bindings use the independent Purpose Context package and preserve native workflow ownership.\n- The fresh visual documents ACTIVATION, SDLC_DEFAULTS and TICKETS with explicit residuals; Lean and the old context/registry routes are retired.\n\n[Install and get started](https://github.com/foolishimp/specification_methodology/blob/c1e0faaa8437c169031a476343c764614135cd93/specification_methodology/v3/plugins/spec/references/GETTING_STARTED.md) · [Skills guide](https://github.com/foolishimp/specification_methodology/blob/f68e8f47db69425205db313ba72fbc9cad94c2b9/stdo_skills/GETTING_STARTED.md) · [Release scope](https://github.com/foolishimp/specification_methodology/blob/f68e8f47db69425205db313ba72fbc9cad94c2b9/releases/3.1.0-rc.1/RELEASE.md) · [Migration](https://github.com/foolishimp/specification_methodology/blob/f68e8f47db69425205db313ba72fbc9cad94c2b9/releases/3.1.0-rc.1/MIGRATION.md)\n\nUse the six attached assets. The native manifest and manager install the Method; `stdo-products-v3.1.0-rc.1.zip` contains the five companion Product directories. The offline manager runtime targets CPython 3.13 on macOS arm64. GitHub's automatic source archive covers the native Method cut; the companion ZIP provides the other Products.\n\nIndependent assessment supports the two exact example queries, with recorded residuals. Both installed host layouts produce matching assessed contexts. The source-matched visual passed independent fidelity review after one bounded correction. Qualification is limited to the declared subjects: it does not establish arbitrary-query coverage, automatic host pickup, code correctness, whole-method semantic completeness or general effectiveness. Existing consumers are not adopted automatically.\n\nNative manifest SHA-256: `ddbd3910981a63f41c17879551f93ef58f369848bae81cc9726d77df55dc7faa`.\n\nThe cohort asset binds all six Product identities, inventories, dependencies, assets and refs. Public acquisition and installation readback are recorded in the postpublication closure linked here when complete.\n"}